---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach OraDiscuss: one email address, answered by the person who writes the material."
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p>
    One address, and it reaches the person who writes the scripts and the briefs rather than a
    queue.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:support@oradiscuss.com">support@oradiscuss.com</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    Use it for support on anything published here, refund requests, privacy and data requests, and
    licensing questions. There is no response time commitment and no service level agreement; see
    the <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> for what support does and does not cover.
  </p>

  <h2>If a script or a course is broken</h2>
  <p>
    Say what you ran, on what version, and what happened. We will fix it and send you the corrected
    version, and if we cannot reproduce the fault we will say so and work with you on what we need.
    Fixes reach every member through the changelog, so a problem you report is a problem everyone
    stops having.
  </p>

  <h2>Billing, invoices and payment questions</h2>
  <p>
    Purchases are sold and billed by a Merchant of Record, currently Paddle.com Market Ltd
    or Lemon Squeezy LLC. The one that sold to you is shown at checkout and on your receipt. Your receipt
    carries a customer portal link where you can find invoices, update your payment method, or
    cancel. For anything about a charge itself, that portal is faster than we are. Refund requests
    can come to either of us; see the <a href="/refund/">Refund Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who operates this site</h2>
  <p>
    OraDiscuss is written and run by an individual practitioner. More about the person and the work
    is on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
